WEBVTT

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.470
Man, that feels good!

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:11.330
Hinata, can you stop messing around and actually help us?

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.620
Sure.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.050
Sheesh.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:19.100
Grandma, we're at the flea-market today.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.130
It looks like the local business board

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.540
organizes one every year to bring the neighborhood together.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.680
Bring that to the front.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.170
Of course, we're selling our paper.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.420
Today's another day to give it my best!

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.860
The First Person

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.200
We made it!

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.790
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.760
You're late!

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.650
I'm sorry, but to make up for it, I made all these tasty things!

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.570
Wow, you made cake!

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.780
Are we selling these too?

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.370
Yeah, we got permission from the board's chief.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.820
Think anyone will want to buy them?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:38.030
I bet they'll sell out right away.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.990
They look so delicious!

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.070
No, they do not <i>look</i> delicious.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.120
They are, without a doubt, undeniably, delicious!

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.020
Thanks Yuuki!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.260
And since you've been helping me since morning,

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.050
here you go!

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.390
Your favorite: cream puffs!

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.190
Oh, you got some...

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.350
Oh, sorry!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.540
Here you go.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.730
Is it good?

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.820
Keep it to a level where you don't get locked up for public indecency.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:19.880
Are these the feng shui products you got from the seminar?

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.170
In order for the yeast-chan to ferment nicely,

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.110
you can't avoid prayer,

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:30.800
and that's after you have done everything in your power.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.720
There's a lot...

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.700
But since you're selling them

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.720
I guess you can't guarantee their effectiveness.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.620
Hey, does this go like this?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.440
No, it goes like this!

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.850
I guess that's not the only thing we have to worry about...

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.380
But with all this,

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:55.620
I bet we'll sell enough stuff to finally buy us some air conditioning!

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.040
Don't you think, everyone?

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.210
No, no, no! Don't think we're getting off that easy!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:04.250
This is still not enough to get the fabled air conditioning.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.270
But then that fabled air conditioning...

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.720
Saki-chan!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.710
And now, my tribute...

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:23.340
Wow, you guys all came!

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.770
How could we not, when you asked us to?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.320
Here you go!

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.860
I asked my mom, and she gave me all these clothes we don't need anymore.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.870
I brought unused tableware.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.750
My dad said you could have his old golf equipment.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.650
I brought a present from my sister's ex...

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.580
Here's some CDs my brother doesn't listen to anymore...

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.750
I got some coupons from my grandmother to Health Land Spa!

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.430
And a bonsai tree from my grandpa!

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.070
Oh, you shouldn't have!

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.380
You really don't mind giving us all these things?

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.390
Of course not!

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.540
We're all rooting for you, Saki-chan!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.020
Thank you so much!

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.070
Now you see our Chief's true powers.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.160
She's amazing.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:15.050
Bye now! See you tomorrow at school!

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:18.860
All right, everyone, get ready to sell your heart out!

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.850
It's air-conditioning or bust!

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.300
I'm collecting eco-points.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.760
Thank you very much!

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.450
There's plenty more where that came from!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.920
See, all you have to do is...

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.680
Oops, maybe it was this way?

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:44.340
That will be 500 yen exactly.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.610
Thank you!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.870
We're doing quite well...

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:53.260
This flea market has kind of become a yearly attraction.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.440
Which reminds me...

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.910
I was walking by here last year and peeked in...

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.710
Hey, remember last year's flea-market,

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.520
when Marimo-chan dropped all that change?

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.350
How could I forget?

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.030
Not only did she not pick it up, she started yelling

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.730
"Finders keepers!",

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:15.290
until we had a veritable stampede on our hands.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:21.130
Yeah, that was awesome!

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:24.480
Yeah, if by "awesome", you mean "sucky".

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.990
Hey, how much is this?

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.790
Hello?

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:34.700
Excuse me one moment!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.190
Excuse me...

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:05.190
I'm very sorry, you were asking about this, right?

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:10.380
You say you want to know how much, but a ten yen coin is ten yen,

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.590
and a one hundred yen coin is one hundred...

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.350
So how much is it?

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.500
I'm going to take a stab

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.710
and say it's probably 110 yen...

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:18.870
Stop right there!

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.000
It costs this much.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.290
I had no idea change was so expensive!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.830
Why?

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:30.140
Very few of these coins were minted and distributed,

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.040
so they are quite rare.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:33.180
Wow, really?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.640
I didn't believe it myself, at first.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:41.080
Wow!!!

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.940
Well, it's for our darling air-conditioning

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:49.270
that I gave up my coin collection babies.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:55.640
And they're still a steal!

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:59.890
You gotta sell high and buy cheap

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:04.300
if you want to make everyone at a flea-market happy!

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:11.340
And then this way, we can finally realize our air-conditioner ambitions!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:17.220
It's, like, bliss for all!

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:21.350
I've already got the pamphlet right here.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.660
Which one should we pick?

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.550
I didn't realize having one was so great.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:30.810
The difference between having and not having one is huge!

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:34.540
For the demons live in the wintry dawn!

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:38.810
That's what they say anyway.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:44.080
Just thinking about it makes me shake, is it the cold or the fear?

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:49.930
Don't worry, I'm right here, so you won't be cold nor afraid!

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:56.000
You're right... Ah, I think I don't care about air conditioning any more.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.630
It looks like they won't need ACs in their room.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.040
Shall we put the extra unit in your room, Kana?

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.400
Oh, I don't need anything that fancy!

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.830
After all, I don't really...

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.630
What are you talking about?

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.980
Oh nothing, really!

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.510
But that reminds me,

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:20.150
I haven't eaten anything since this morning,

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:21.890
so I've been getting hungrier and hungrier...

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:22.770
Oh?

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:25.630
Shall we start taking lunch breaks?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:26.700
Okay!

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:27.880
Kana?

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.010
Yes?

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:31.750
Can you also get us some change, while you're out?

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.130
All right.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:42.460
Kana, you're here too?

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:43.180
Uh-huh.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.960
What's wrong? You're not your normal self.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.210
That's not true. I'm fine, just fine!

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:51.940
Are you running a booth at the flea-market too?

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:57.150
Yeah, but there I was, all raring to help,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.930
and they told me I should just go already and get lunch!

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.190
Did you do something?

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.650
Not a thing!

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:13.170
But there are so many angry customers at this flea market thing.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.080
Is that so...

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:21.260
Well, if you insist, I guess we can have lunch together.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.920
All right.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.790
Kana?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:25.660
Huh?

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.410
All right.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:30.850
But I was asked to get some change as well,

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.030
so I'll have to go to the bank first.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.190
Okay.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.750
I've got a plan!

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:39.360
Since my booth told me I don't have to go back anyway,

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.820
why don't I help at the Fuhshin booth while you're getting lunch?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.140
I'll be waiting at the Fuhshin booth!

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.270
Okay, see you later!

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:03.600
Uh-oh!

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.260
I'm sorry!

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:11.440
Is your cute little butt all right?

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.490
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:32.960
This is all because I wasn't paying attention!

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.030
Yup, we've got some tasty veggies!

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.680
Will you put them out?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:54.790
That's right, step right up, ladies and gentlemen!

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:59.780
They may look a little banged up, but they're all fresh.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.770
All picked this morning, and just ten yen each!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.190
These please.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.090
Yes ma'am. Thank you.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:11.740
I'd like these please, and some...

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.930
I actually don't...

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.440
These cucumbers too, please!

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:16.610
I'm next!

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.170
I'd like these peppers and tomatoes.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.880
These onions and pumpkins and that!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.180
You ham actor.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.280
Thank you very much!

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:27.150
Wow, talk about the power of discounts!

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:29.220
Here you go!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:33.220
Oh, you don't have to, I didn't...

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.600
Thank you.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.680
It's delicious!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.750
Really? I'm glad.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.170
All right, then I'm...

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.280
Are you going home?

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.610
Of course not!

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:51.910
My truck's parked right over there, so shall we?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.940
Umm...!

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.500
There are a lot of veggies still left!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.460
What I meant was...

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.720
Isn't the rice ball I made with my rice good?

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:05.690
Yes.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.030
<b>Then</b>

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:17.760
Step right up!

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:21.310
Uhm, well... uhmmm!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.540
It's all for sale...!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.780
Here you go.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:34.390
Welcome.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.110
Please buy a lot.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:38.150
They're cheap!

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:43.480
This is the last!

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.620
Thank you so much.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:46.720
I'll be on my way then...

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.940
Can I interest you in some fresh-picked vegetables?

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.760
They're 10 yen each.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.730
Oh really?

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.930
I can make you a real steal!

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.830
How about you take the rest, for 100 yen?

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:02.480
I would, if I could get them home somehow.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.820
That's not a problem.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.460
We'll deliver them.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.770
Oh really?

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.010
Thank you so much!

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:13.160
Thank you again!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.220
Oh, it was nothing!

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.660
Our pleasure!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.180
Goodbye!

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:24.670
I guess they were all discounted in the end, but did it go all right?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:31.460
Not really, to be honest, but the customers seemed happy.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.180
Umm, the way back is this way.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:53.560
Umm... I'm going to get lost!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.140
Please wait!

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.470
What are you doing?

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:21.560
That's someone's house!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.890
You recognize this scent too?

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:34.790
Are you talking to Bunta?

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.860
Please wait!

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:51.000
Please... wait!

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:53.430
You're doing that again?

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.620
I guess since this is a temple and not a private house,

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.400
it's all right to enter. Right?

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.400
Excuse my intrusion!

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.280
This is...

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.190
Come here.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:34.640
The flea-market grounds are over there.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:40.030
And I think the newspaper where I used to work is thataway.

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.460
You worked for a newspaper?

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.330
That's right.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.450
Up until last year.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:54.430
Actually, I'm working for a newspaper too!

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:57.230
Really?

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.580
Yeah.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.050
Oh, a sweet olive tree!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.140
Yeah.

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:14.570
Doesn't it smell good?

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:15.470
It does!

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:19.670
So you were following this scent the whole time?

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:20.470
Yup.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.080
Wasn't it fun?

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:35.410
Umm, I work for a newspaper too.

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.530
I know. You said that before.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:45.610
I still can't ride a bike though, or deliver a lot of papers.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:49.500
I keep thinking... that I'm pretty useless,

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:53.580
and I wonder how long I'll be allowed to stay.

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:02.080
From, far away;

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:06.940
From an island without a name,

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:14.830
Floats a single, lonesome coconut

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:22.530
Far from the shores of its home.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:31.730
How many moons did it ride the waves?

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:40.480
Maybe the old tree is growing strong,

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:48.820
its branches casting shadows.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:56.780
I continue my lonesome journey as well,

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:05.490
the beach my pillow, the water my bed.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.030
Coconut...

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:13.180
I know that song, it's...

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:15.660
Doesn't being a coconut sound like fun?

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:16.290
Huh?

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.220
Isn't traveling nice?

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:22.180
Go where the wind takes you, where your mood takes you.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:26.810
You go to all these places and meet all these people.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:32.570
You're in the middle of a journey too, aren't you?

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:43.070
Oh no, is this because you hate coconuts?

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:47.710
Oh. You don't like coconut milk, do you?

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:50.810
Then that jelliness of Nata de coco...

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:54.610
I do like coconuts!

00:19:55.900 --> 00:20:00.530
Co, co, co, what about cocoa?

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:01.620
An ice cream!

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:02.720
Many steamed buns!

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:06.210
In this word-game, if you say a word that ends in "n", you lose.

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:06.210
I lost!

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:07.970
I won!

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:16.730
My name is Kana Nakamachi. What's your name?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.780
Aren't they heavy?

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.340
Thanks for all your help today!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.860
No, I should be thanking you.

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.040
People are just like vegetables...

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:53.370
When the right season comes, they will bloom and bear fruit.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.490
You'll get there too.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:56.510
Thanks!

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:07.490
Even though it's kind of a sad song about leaving your home,

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:11.980
she said it was a fun song about going on a journey.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:16.750
She laughed and told me I was in the middle of my journey, too.

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:21.380
I'm laughing, Grandma!

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.140
There she is!

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:27.730
Because you didn't bring us change from the bank,

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:30.910
our business, our business, our business!

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:34.310
Paycut! Paycut! Paycut!

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:37.750
I'm sorry!

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:54.440
Grandma, I met a magician today.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:58.300
Could that person possibly have been...?

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:44.860
And the first...

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:33.900
Next time, our last episode will be "And the first..."

00:23:33.900 --> 00:23:35.240
Hey, Kana.

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:37.180
What's wrong?

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:39.170
Hey, Kana...

00:23:39.170 --> 00:23:40.670
It'll be the last episode.

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:43.360
That's too sudden, Mika-chan!
